{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact integration head 0bac8fd1d512323e329731a192802454483925fe (one release commit atop the two already-approved heads merged into integrate/release-gap-closure; the three carried files - sample HTML, sample PNG, conservative-upgrade note - are byte-identical to their approved heads c3e4748 and 4b77d44f; not on main). Judged against the operator umbrella #2270 verbatim. TAG GATES: release.yml keeps the exact-tag, semver, and merged-main checks and reruns test/race/vet before building; elevated permissions now live only on the tag-push job, PRs run a read-only release-dry-run job that builds unsigned assets and asserts install.sh, checksums.txt, SHA256SUMS exist - the earlier advisory, closed. ARTIFACTS: four darwin/linux arm64/amd64 archives containing tailapp, LICENSE, NOTICE; checksums.txt plus an identical SHA256SUMS; Cosign bundle and signature on the checksum manifest; GitHub provenance attestations; and the NEW version-pinned install.sh asset rendered by release.sh from scripts/install.sh with the release version substituted (the checkout copy refuses to run unrendered), listed in the checksum manifests, and published by gh release create dist/*. VERSION COMMAND: tailapp version prints one JSON object (version, revision, dirty, source_url, go_version, os, arch) from build metadata without touching TAILAPP_HOME or a resident; verified on the built binary (0.1.0+0bac8fd1d512, revision, dirty false, sanitized source URL) and, via the installer test, on a stamped release binary (version 0.0.0-test); ldflag stamping unchanged and tested. INSTALLER AS RELEASE CONSUMER: install.sh downloads the matching archive, checksums.txt, .sig and .bundle from the pinned release URL, requires a 64-hex entry and an exact SHA-256 match, verifies the keyless signature identity for that exact tag when cosign is present (warns explicitly when not), smoke-runs the extracted binary with version, installs to \u003croot\u003e/lib/tailapp/tailapp-\u00